    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d401">

                <pb facs="0780" n="660" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg660"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.1120 H 87/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-11T13:00:00-03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 11,
                                1922—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:12 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>87. Department’s 89 July 24, 4 p.m.<anchor n="22" xml:id="d401-f1"/> Brazilian
                    Foreign Office informed me to-day that Secretary of State in his character as
                    dean <pb facs="0781" n="661" xml:id="pg661"/> of special ambassadors to the
                    centennial celebration will be requested to speak in the name of his colleagues
                    at a dinner given by President of Brazil on September 9th. He will also be
                    requested to speak at a dinner to special ambassadors offered by Brazilian
                    Government on September 10th over which Minister for Foreign Affairs will not
                    preside and at which President of Brazil will probably not be present.<anchor
                        n="23" xml:id="d401-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d401-f1" n="22" xml:id="d401-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d401-f2" n="23" xml:id="d401-f2-content">
                <p>The four speeches made by the Secretary of State were published in <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Addresses in Brazil Delivered by the Hon. Charles Evans
                        Hughes, Secretary of State, September, 1922</hi> (Washington, The Pan
                    American Union, 1922).</p>
            </note>
